// Cells, north to south: the Secteur Eta gate (y 0-1), S7-D the Passerelle des Paradoxes (x 13-15,
// y 2-21, four reversal-tile motifs), S7-C the Pile du Milieu (y 22-35), S7-B the arrow puzzle (the
// source's grid at (9, 36)), S7-A the Culee sud (y 45-71, block C1 alone on y 62). The return chute
// (15-20, 35), (20, 36-45), (18-20, 46): slide arrows from the foot of S7-C down to S7-A, one way south
// (the puzzle cannot be walked back), entered only from (14, 35) or (15, 34), below Sc02's row.
// SilRouteS07 (gfx/SilRouteS07.ron): the data-fog void (2x2), negative by the gate (i j k l), violet in
// S7-D (y z Y X), indigo in S7-C and S7-B (m n o p), dawn pink in S7-A (u v w x); the glass walkway g
// with its violet reversal slabs R (MB_SLIDE_SOUTH), S7-C's steel deck a, the concrete deck c with the logic arrows N Z E W
// (MB_SLIDE_NORTH, SOUTH, EAST, WEST), crystal grass h, broken pylons q r t, Cocket barriers B, screens S
// (signs), the Secteur Eta gate G H I / J P K (P the passage, warp 0). Concrete piers under the decks
